WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.669
Film Courage: Going back to curiosity, which
is more crucial [to you as filmmakers]?

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:08.960
An interesting topic but a reluctant or not
so fully developed subject (for whatever reason)?

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:16.360
Or the reverse, a fascinating person but a
topic that is more vague and little bit too

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:17.360
broad?

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.710
Heidi Ewing: Well, we don’t make films about
topics.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:22.410
We’re very careful not to come up with a
topic and then try to back into it.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:29.370
But it’s important to have subject matter
that is rich and has depth, that it could

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:34.540
be full of surprises and twists and turns,
but it doesn’t matter if you have that in-depth

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:38.380
topic if you don’t have amazing characters
to take you on the journey.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.030
So really we look for both.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:44.000
We look for subject matter that hasn’t been
picked over so many times that people think

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.560
that they know that much about it.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.880
And you also need these great storytellers,
which is part of our casting process, to find

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:56.340
those who can articulate a journey or can
change over the course of a film and bring

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.910
a subject matter to life.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:02.070
Rachel Grady: I think it would be almost a
Venn diagram actually when you put it that

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.070
way.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:07.060
Which is, if there are both, we make a movie
about it.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.840
And it’s hard to have both.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:14.340
It’s unusual, which is why we make a film
every couple of years or so because they don’t

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.840
come along every minute.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.150
Film Courage: How far into the process of
the film do you know if the subject working?

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:23.670
I know Heidi you’d talked previously about
with [their film] The Boys of Baraka that

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:28.380
you had one subject that seemed more reluctant
but that person appeared so fascinating that

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.420
you really wanted to keep up with it [the
filming].

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.370
Heidi Ewing: Yeah…it was a mistake.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.150
Film Courage: Okay…and I’m sure that was
a painful mistake because I’m sure you really

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.150
wanted that person in the film?

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.230
Heidi Ewing: Very much, Dewon.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.520
The one the got away.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:44.550
We have learned over a long career that reluctant
subjects are no subjects at all.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.780
A reluctant subject only exists in your mind.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:55.570
He or she will never participate or allow
you the access that we need in order to make

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:57.049
a satisfying film.

00:01:57.049 --> 00:02:02.549
So we detect very early on by doing test shoots
and allowing people to say “Listen, let’s

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:06.190
come into your house, let’s shoot a little
and see how it feels for both of us?”

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:11.630
Because a reluctant or a subject that is too
shy or camera shy or too self-conscious probably

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.600
won’t get over that and so you have to move
on.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:19.459
And it can be very, very painful and we don’t
really make that mistake too much anymore.

00:02:19.459 --> 00:02:22.340
On this film [ONE OF US documentary] we did
film several people before we settled on our

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:29.380
final three and one was a reluctant subject
that we spent a couple, too many days on (maybe)

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.440
thinking that he might come around but he
did not.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.840
So you keep making those stumbles.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.749
Hopefully you spend less and less time on
the reluctant subject every film.

